-- 188 — WARM AMBIENT. 60 BPM, A minor. No percussion at all: it is harmony, drones, and space.
--
-- Stock Tidal. Orbits -> hardware through the minimal master; orbit FX are the stock
-- dirt_delay -> dirt_reverb -> dirt_monitor, so warmth has to come from VOICES and ENVELOPES
-- rather than from a magic master setting.
--
-- WHY IT IS WARM, concretely:
--   * voices chosen for body not edge: superhammond (organ), orkRhodes/hoRhodes (tine), cb3/cb4
--     (bowed strings from sc/samples115.scd), sprvibe (glass) — no saw, no PWM, nothing with a
--     hard attack
--   * long envelopes: attack 1.2-2.5 s, release 4-8 s. Slow attacks are the single biggest
--     contributor to "warm" — they remove the transient that reads as brightness
--   * filters low and static-ish: lpf 2000-5000, not sweeping highs
--   * minor ninths and no thirds in the bass: Am9 / Fmaj9 / Cmaj9 / G9, i-VI-III-VII
--   * everything wet: room 0.75-0.95, size 0.95, dry 0.25-0.35, plus a long delay on orbit 2
--   * a tempo slow enough that chords overlap: 60 BPM, one chord per TWO bars = 8 s per chord,
--     with 4-8 s releases the harmony never stops sounding
--
-- ORBITS: 0 pad/harmony | 1 drone (bowed, dry-ish so the low end stays defined) | 2 melody +
-- glass into the long delay.
setcps (60/240)

-- HARMONY: superhammond, one chord per two bars, attack 1.2 / release 6. Warm and continuous.
d1 $ slow 2 $ sometimesBy 0.12 (|+ note 12) $ note "<[a3,c4,e4,g4,b4] [f3,a3,c4,e4,g4] [c3,e3,g3,b3,d4] [g3,b3,d4,f4,a4]>" # s "superhammond" # orbit 0 # gain (slow 11 $ range 0.34 0.44 sine) # amp 0.42 # attack 1.2 # release 6 # sustain 0.8 # cutoff (slow 21 $ rangex 1400 3200 saw) # hpf 150 # lpf 5200 # pan (slow 17 $ range 0.44 0.56 sine) # room 0.85 # size 0.95 # dry 0.3

-- DRONE: bowed strings (cb3/cb4 from samples115) holding the root, near-dry so the bottom stays
-- readable under all that reverb.
d2 $ slow 4 $ note "<a1 f1 c2 g1>" # s "<cb3 cb4>" # orbit 1 # gain (slow 13 $ range 0.3 0.4 sine) # hpf 60 # lpf 1800 # pan 0.5 # room 0.25 # size 0.7 # dry 0.8 # release 3

-- WARM MELODY: orkRhodes fragments, sparse and phrased, an octave above the pad, into the delay.
d3 $ mask (slow 8 "<t f t f>") $ slow 4 $ degradeBy 0.25 $ sometimesBy 0.15 (|+ note 12) $ note "<e5 ~ ~ a4 ~ c5 ~ ~ b4 ~ g4 ~ e4 ~ ~ ~ a4 ~ c5 ~ e5 ~ ~ d5 ~ b4 ~ a4 ~ ~ ~>" # s "orkRhodes" # orbit 2 # gain (slow 9 $ range 0.26 0.36 sine) # amp 0.45 # attack 0.35 # release 3 # sustain 0.6 # cutoff 3000 # hpf 300 # lpf 4600 # pan (slow 19 $ range 0.4 0.6 sine) # room 0.7 # size 0.95 # dry 0.4 # delay 0.4 # delaytime (3/8) # delayfeedback 0.55 # lock 1

-- AIR: glass fragments, very quiet, long delay — the top of the space rather than a voice in it.
d4 $ slow 8 $ degradeBy 0.5 $ every 5 (within (0.5,1) (rev)) $ note "<a5 ~ ~ e5 ~ ~ c6 ~ ~ g5 ~ ~ e5 ~ ~ ~>" # s "sprvibe" # n 0 # orbit 2 # gain (slow 23 $ range 0.08 0.16 sine) # hpf 900 # lpf 9000 # release 2.5 # sustain 0.4 # pan (slow 7 $ range 0.3 0.7 sine) # room 0.9 # size 0.98 # dry 0.2 # delay 0.45 # delaytime (3/8) # delayfeedback 0.6 # lock 1
